{"route":"/docs/5.2/utilities/spacing/","version":"5.2","renderedVersion":"5.2","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Spacing","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap includes a wide range of shorthand responsive margin, padding, and gap utility classes to modify an element’s appearance."},"blocks":[{"id":"margin-and-padding","type":"heading","en":"Margin and padding","level":2},{"id":"margin-and-padding--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Assign responsive-friendly <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> values to an element or a subset of its sides with shorthand classes. Includes support for individual properties, all properties, and vertical and horizontal properties. Classes are built from a default Sass map ranging from <code>.25rem</code> to <code>3rem</code>."},{"id":"margin-and-padding--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"margin-and-padding--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Using the CSS Grid layout module?</strong> Consider using <a href=\"#gap\">the gap utility</a> instead."}]},{"id":"notation","type":"heading","en":"Notation","level":3},{"id":"notation--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Spacing utilities that apply to all breakpoints, from <code>xs</code> to <code>xxl</code>, have no breakpoint abbreviation in them. This is because those classes are applied from <code>min-width: 0</code> and up, and thus are not bound by a media query. The remaining breakpoints, however, do include a breakpoint abbreviation."},{"id":"notation--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The classes are named using the format <code>{property}{sides}-{size}</code> for <code>xs</code> and <code>{property}{sides}-{breakpoint}-{size}</code> for <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>lg</code>, <code>xl</code>, and <code>xxl</code>."},{"id":"notation--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>property</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>m</code> - for classes that set <code>margin</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>p</code> - for classes that set <code>padding</code>"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>sides</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-2","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>t</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-top</code> or <code>padding-top</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-4","type":"item","en":"<code>b</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-bottom</code> or <code>padding-bottom</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-5","type":"item","en":"<code>s</code> - (start) for classes that set <code>margin-left</code> or <code>padding-left</code> in LTR, <code>margin-right</code> or <code>padding-right</code> in RTL"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-6","type":"item","en":"<code>e</code> - (end) for classes that set <code>margin-right</code> or <code>padding-right</code> in LTR, <code>margin-left</code> or <code>padding-left</code> in RTL"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-7","type":"item","en":"<code>x</code> - for classes that set both <code>*-left</code> and <code>*-right</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-8","type":"item","en":"<code>y</code> - for classes that set both <code>*-top</code> and <code>*-bottom</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-9","type":"item","en":"blank - for classes that set a <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> on all 4 sides of the element"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>size</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-3","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-10","type":"item","en":"<code>0</code> - for classes that eliminate the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> by setting it to <code>0</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-11","type":"item","en":"<code>1</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * .25</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-12","type":"item","en":"<code>2</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * .5</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-13","type":"item","en":"<code>3</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-14","type":"item","en":"<code>4</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * 1.5</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-15","type":"item","en":"<code>5</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * 3</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-16","type":"item","en":"<code>auto</code> - for classes that set the <code>margin</code> to auto"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"(You can add more sizes by adding entries to the <code>$spacers</code> Sass map variable.)"},{"id":"examples","type":"heading","en":"Examples","level":3},{"id":"examples--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Here are some representative examples of these classes:"},{"id":"examples--code-1","type":"code","value":".mt-0 {\n  margin-top: 0 !important;\n}\n\n.ms-1 {\n  margin-left: ($spacer * .25) !important;\n}\n\n.px-2 {\n  padding-left: ($spacer * .5) !important;\n  padding-right: ($spacer * .5) !important;\n}\n\n.p-3 {\n  padding: $spacer !important;\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"horizontal-centering","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal centering","level":3},{"id":"horizontal-centering--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Additionally, Bootstrap also includes an <code>.mx-auto</code> class for horizontally centering fixed-width block level content—that is, content that has <code>display: block</code> and a <code>width</code> set—by setting the horizontal margins to <code>auto</code>."},{"id":"horizontal-centering--example-1","type":"demo","key":"31610befc8ef99ed277c","height":147},{"id":"horizontal-centering--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"mx-auto\" style=\"width: 200px;\">\n  Centered element\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"negative-margin","type":"heading","en":"Negative margin","level":2},{"id":"negative-margin--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"In CSS, <code>margin</code> properties can utilize negative values (<code>padding</code> cannot). These negative margins are <strong>disabled by default</strong>, but can be enabled in Sass by setting <code>$enable-negative-margins: true</code>."},{"id":"negative-margin--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The syntax is nearly the same as the default, positive margin utilities, but with the addition of <code>n</code> before the requested size. Here’s an example class that’s the opposite of <code>.mt-1</code>:"},{"id":"negative-margin--code-1","type":"code","value":".mt-n1 {\n  margin-top: -0.25rem !important;\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"gap","type":"heading","en":"Gap","level":2},{"id":"gap--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"When using <code>display: grid</code>, you can make use of <code>gap</code> utilities on the parent grid container. This can save on having to add margin utilities to individual grid items (children of a <code>display: grid</code> container). Gap utilities are responsive by default, and are generated via our utilities API, based on the <code>$spacers</code> Sass map."},{"id":"gap--example-1","type":"demo","key":"2918c4bb24bc51d6340b","height":147},{"id":"gap--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"d-grid gap-3\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 1</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 2</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 3</div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"gap--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Support includes responsive options for all of Bootstrap’s grid breakpoints, as well as six sizes from the <code>$spacers</code> map (<code>0</code>–<code>5</code>). There is no <code>.gap-auto</code> utility class as it’s effectively the same as <code>.gap-0</code>."},{"id":"sass","type":"heading","en":"Sass","level":2},{"id":"maps","type":"heading","en":"Maps","level":3},{"id":"maps--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Spacing utilities are declared via Sass map and then generated with our utilities API."},{"id":"maps--code-1","type":"code","value":"$spacer: 1rem;\n$spacers: (\n  0: 0,\n  1: $spacer * .25,\n  2: $spacer * .5,\n  3: $spacer,\n  4: $spacer * 1.5,\n  5: $spacer * 3,\n);","language":"scss"},{"id":"utilities-api","type":"heading","en":"Utilities API","level":3},{"id":"utilities-api--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Spacing utilities are declared in our utilities API in <code>scss/_utilities.scss</code>. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/utilities/api/#using-the-api\">Learn how to use the utilities API.</a>"},{"id":"utilities-api--code-1","type":"code","value":"    \"margin\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin,\n      class: m,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-x\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-right margin-left,\n      class: mx,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-y\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-top margin-bottom,\n      class: my,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-top\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-top,\n      class: mt,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-end\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-right,\n      class: me,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-bottom\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-bottom,\n      class: mb,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    \"margin-start\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-left,\n      class: ms,\n      values: map-merge($spacers, (auto: auto))\n    ),\n    // Negative margin utilities\n    \"negative-margin\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin,\n      class: m,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-x\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-right margin-left,\n      class: mx,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-y\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-top margin-bottom,\n      class: my,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-top\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-top,\n      class: mt,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-end\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-right,\n      class: me,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-bottom\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-bottom,\n      class: mb,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    \"negative-margin-start\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: margin-left,\n      class: ms,\n      values: $negative-spacers\n    ),\n    // Padding utilities\n    \"padding\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding,\n      class: p,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-x\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-right padding-left,\n      class: px,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-y\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-top padding-bottom,\n      class: py,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-top\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-top,\n      class: pt,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-end\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-right,\n      class: pe,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-bottom\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-bottom,\n      class: pb,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    \"padding-start\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: padding-left,\n      class: ps,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),\n    // Gap utility\n    \"gap\": (\n      responsive: true,\n      property: gap,\n      class: gap,\n      values: $spacers\n    ),","language":"scss"}],"demos":[{"key":"31610befc8ef99ed277c","html":"\n  <div class=\"mx-auto\" style=\"width: 200px; background-color: rgba(86,61,124,.15);\">\n    Centered element\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"2918c4bb24bc51d6340b","html":"\n<div class=\"d-grid gap-3\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 1</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 2</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-light border\">Grid item 3</div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/parcel/"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/vite/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/rfs/"},{"en":"RTL","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/rtl/"},{"en":"Contribute